// Labeled cases for `wstack skill-suggest --eval .wrongstack/skill-suggest-eval.jsonl --sweep`
//
// DRAFT. Every `gold` below is inferred from the skill's own frontmatter
// trigger, not from knowing how you actually work. Correct them before you
// trust any number this produces — a wrong label counts against the suggester
// on every run.
//
// Shape: {"text": "...", "gold": "skill-name"}  — a skill covers this request
//        {"text": "..."}                        — nothing in the roster covers it
//
// The uncovered half is not filler. A set made only of covered requests will
// score ~90% and tell you nothing, because the failure this feature actually
// has is suggesting something on turns where nothing fits.
//
// KNOWN LABEL PROBLEM: the mailbox trio below (wrongstack-mailbox /
// wrongstack-mailbox-mcp / mailbox-bridge) accounts for most of the residual
// "wrong suggestion" rate. Measured runs keep picking mailbox-bridge for all
// three. That may be the labels rather than the suggester — decide what you
// actually mean by each and either fix the labels or drop the pair.
//
// Deliberately ABSENT: the design-system / design-craft / design-critique
// trio on "restyle"-style requests. `design-craft` says to use it "alongside
// design-system", and all three list the same trigger words, so there is no
// single right answer to score against. See docs/skills-suggestion.md.

// ── covered: review family (four skills, genuinely close) ───────────────────
{"text": "review the changes on this branch before I open a pull request", "gold": "code-review"}
{"text": "go through the diff on this PR and tell me what would block it", "gold": "code-review"}
{"text": "scan src/coordination for anti-patterns and code smells", "gold": "bug-hunter"}
{"text": "look over everything we touched this session for quality problems", "gold": "chimera"}
{"text": "how do I turn off the auto-review plugin and see what it flagged", "gold": "auto-review"}
{"text": "check this config for security vulnerabilities", "gold": "security-scanner"}

// ── covered: debugging vs bug-hunter (broken-now vs scan-for-latent) ────────
{"text": "this test passes locally but fails in CI and I have no idea why", "gold": "debugging"}
{"text": "the daemon crashes on startup with a null deref, find the cause", "gold": "debugging"}

